%% The blast radius of one real regression (ExplainabilityForce, D053): impact_of.cypher starts at the new decision and follows edges outward; every box is one row with a reason.
flowchart LR
  N["New decision: reopened<br/>8 Mar · 'customer CUST-0011 has<br/>reopened the bug ...'"]:::guard
  O["Replaced decision: resolved<br/>7 Mar → 8 Mar"]:::store
  M["Message that said fixed<br/>'... has been resolved. You can<br/>check the details in the PR'"]:::file
  I["Issue: Improper Authentication<br/>Token Validation<br/>API Security Module"]:::store
  PR["PR 57 (merged)<br/>Fix: Proper Validation of<br/>Authentication Tokens"]:::file
  DT["David Taylor, Software Engineer<br/>authored the fix · assignee ·<br/>said it was resolved"]:::human
  BD["Bob Davis, Engineering Lead<br/>reviewed: APPROVED"]:::human
  CU["Paul Brown (CUST-0011)<br/>reported the issue"]:::human
  CO["DataSolutions<br/>the customer's company"]:::ext
  SIB["4 sibling issues, same component<br/>resolved / dismissed → recheck"]:::store
  T["2 teams WORKS_ON<br/>ExplainabilityForce"]:::human
  N -- "SUPERSEDES" --> O
  O -- "EVIDENCED_BY" --> M
  O -- "DECIDED_BY" --> DT
  N -- "AFFECTS" --> I
  PR -- "FIXES" --> I
  DT -- "AUTHORED" --> PR
  BD -- "REVIEWED" --> PR
  I -- "REPORTED_BY" --> CU
  CU -- "WORKS_AT" --> CO
  I -. "same component" .-> SIB
  I -. "IN_PRODUCT ← WORKS_ON" .-> T
